-      "title": "RAG hybrid retrieval with BM25 and cross-encoder reranking for knowledge base",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Upgrade the Rainbow AI knowledge base retrieval pipeline from pure vector similarity search to hybrid retrieval combining lexical (BM25) and semantic (vector) search, followed by a cross-encoder reranker. Hybrid retrieval outperforms pure vector search for domain-specific hospitality and FnB queries where exact-match terms (room names, dish names, prices) matter. Optimal chunk size is 200â€“500 tokens with 10â€“20% overlap.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Knowledge base queries use both BM25 keyword ranking and vector cosine similarity, merged via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)",
-        "A cross-encoder reranker re-scores the top-20 candidates before selecting the top-3 context chunks",
-        "Chunk size for .rainbow-kb/ files is 300 tokens (Â±50) with 15% overlap on split",
-        "Retrieval latency for a KB query is â‰¤500ms at P95",
-        "Retrieval quality is evaluated monthly using nDCG on a curated test set of 50 known Q&A pairs",
-        "If no KB chunk scores above the relevance threshold (default 0.65), the system falls back to the AI provider without injecting context"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Hybrid search: combine BM25 (via pg_bm25/ParadeDB or Elasticsearch) with pgvector cosine similarity",
-        "Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF): score = Î£ 1/(k + rank_i) where k=60",
-        "Cross-encoder reranker: ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 or similar lightweight model",
-        "Evaluation: RAGAS framework for end-to-end faithfulness and context precision metrics",
-        "Reference: https://stackoverflow.blog/2024/08/15/practical-tips-for-retrieval-augmented-generation-rag/"
