-      "id": "US-927",
-      "title": "WhatsApp Flows: upgrade endpoint to Data API version 4.0 two-signature auth",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Meta released WhatsApp Flows Data API v4.0 in November 2025 introducing a two-signature authentication mechanism. The second signature is an optional flow token signature that businesses can verify to confirm requests originate from WhatsApp and have not been tampered with. Upgrading to v4.0 in Flow JSON hardens the existing encrypted data-exchange endpoint against replay and forgery attacks â€” particularly important for the guest digital check-in flow that handles personal data.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "All WhatsApp Flow JSON files served by Rainbow AI have data_api_version set to '4.0'",
-        "The Flows endpoint handler verifies the platform-side HMAC signature on every incoming request",
-        "Optionally, the flow token signature is also verified when RAINBOW_FLOWS_VERIFY_TOKEN_SIG=true is set",
-        "A rejected signature returns HTTP 401 and logs a security event with flow_id and timestamp",
-        "Existing flow functionality (check-in form, reservation form) is not broken after upgrade",
-        "Unit test covers: valid signature passes, tampered body is rejected, missing signature is rejected"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Set data_api_version: '4.0' in Flow JSON â€” no functional behavior change, only security enhancement",
-        "Platform signature: HMAC-SHA256 of request body using app secret",
-        "Flow token signature: optional second HMAC for business-side token verification",
-        "Reference: WhatsApp Flows Changelog, November 11 2025 entry"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [
