-    {
-      "id": "US-941",
-      "title": "Migrate Baileys auth state to production-safe database store",
-      "priority": "critical",
-      "description": "Baileys v7.0.0 explicitly prohibits useMultiFileAuthState in production due to excessive I/O, and v7 introduces mandatory support for three new auth state keys (lid-mapping, device-list, tctoken) required by WhatsApp's LID system. Without a proper database-backed auth store (PostgreSQL/Redis), the production instance will have broken credentials persistence, session rejections, and reconnect loops. This is a breaking migration from v6 to v7.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Auth state is persisted in PostgreSQL using a custom store (not useMultiFileAuthState) that handles the creds.update event",
-        "New Baileys v7 required keys (lid-mapping, device-list, tctoken) are stored and retrieved correctly",
-        "On server restart, WhatsApp connection resumes without requiring a new QR scan",
-        "Connection drops with restartRequired status code trigger socket recreation (not socket reuse)",
-        "No 401 device_removed reconnect loops in production logs over a 24-hour period"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Baileys v7 switched from CommonJS to ESM exclusively â€” dynamic import() required if host module is CJS",
-        "The isPnUser() function replaces removed isJidUser(); Contact type now uses a single id field with separate phoneNumber and lid fields",
-        "ACK on delivery was removed â€” WhatsApp bans users for sending ACKs; remove any manual ACK logic",
-        "Reference: https://baileys.wiki/docs/migration/to-v7.0.0/",
-        "Community package: https://github.com/rzkytmgr/baileysauth (supports pg, MongoDB, Redis)"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "large",
-      "passes": true
-    },
