-    {
-      "id": "US-962",
-      "title": "Detect and handle portfolio pacing pause signals for batch sends",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "WhatsApp now batches large template campaigns and monitors quality signals (blocks, reports, engagement) before releasing subsequent batches. If negative signals appear, remaining messages in the batch may not be sent without warning. The system currently has no mechanism to detect pacing pauses, alert operators, or retry/requeue affected messages â€” meaning silent delivery failures during campaign sends.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Webhook handler processes the `message_status: failed` event with error code 131049 (frequency-cap saturation) and distinguishes it from hard delivery failures",
-        "Admin dashboard shows a 'Pacing Pause' alert when more than 5% of a batch is held, including the affected batch ID and message count",
-        "Operator receives a notification (webhook or email) when a campaign send is paused by portfolio pacing",
-        "Held messages are not silently discarded; they are queued for operator review with a re-send or cancel action",
-        "System exposes a pacing health metric in the analytics dashboard (messages held vs delivered per campaign)"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Error 131049 = frequency-cap / pacing pause; Error 130429 or 131057 = throughput/speed issues",
-        "Portfolio pacing applies to accounts with <500K messages/year or showing suspicious quality signals",
-        "Reference: https://woztell.com/whatsapp-api-2026-updates-pacing-limits-usernames/ and https://sanuker.com/whatsapp-api-2026_updates-pacing-limits-usernames/"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-963",
-      "title": "Implement per-message cost model with free CSW utility window tracking",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Since July 1, 2025, WhatsApp shifted from conversation-based to per-template-message pricing. Utility template messages sent within an active 24-hour Customer Service Window (CSW) are now free; the same templates sent outside the window are charged the utility rate. The existing per-message cost capture story captures cost per message, but does not implement the CSW-window logic to correctly categorize and zero-cost utility messages sent within the window â€” leading to overstated cost estimates.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "System tracks the start time of each customer's active CSW (triggered by any inbound user message)",
-        "Utility template messages dispatched within the CSW are tagged `cost: 0` in the message cost ledger",
-        "Utility templates sent after CSW expiry are charged at the standard utility rate for the user's country",
-        "Marketing templates are always charged regardless of CSW status",
-        "Authentication templates are always charged individually regardless of CSW status",
-        "Cost dashboard correctly displays zero-cost utility messages as a separate line from charged utility messages",
-        "Volume-tier discounts (Utility and Authentication only) are applied correctly once monthly thresholds are reached"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "CSW starts on the last inbound message from the user and expires 24 hours later",
-        "Free utility window only applies to template messages, not service (freeform) messages â€” those are always free",
-        "Volume tiers apply per WABA per country; reference: https://www.eesel.ai/blog/whatsapp-business-api-latest-pricing-and-policy-changes",
-        "Marketing templates are never free regardless of CSW; utility upsells/cross-sells risk reclassification as Marketing"
-      ],
