-    {
-      "id": "US-964",
-      "title": "Enforce marketing message frequency cap and surface error 131049",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Meta enforces a user-level frequency cap: each WhatsApp user can receive at most approximately 2 marketing template messages per 10-day rolling period from all businesses combined. When this cap is exceeded, the Cloud API returns error code 131049 and the message is silently undelivered. The current system does not surface this error distinctly to operators, who may incorrectly attribute the failure to connectivity or QoS issues.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "On receiving error 131049 from the Cloud API, the message is marked `status: undelivered_frequency_cap` rather than a generic failure",
-        "Admin dashboard shows a distinct 'Frequency Cap Reached' failure reason in the message log",
-        "Campaign analytics display frequency-cap failures as a separate metric from network failures or policy violations",
-        "When >10% of a campaign batch fails with 131049, an operator alert fires within 5 minutes",
-        "Re-send logic does not automatically retry messages that failed with 131049 within the same 10-day window"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Cap is approximately 2 marketing templates per user per 10-day window from ALL businesses, not just yours",
-        "Click-to-WhatsApp ads are exempt from frequency capping",
-        "Error 131049 is returned as a standard Cloud API delivery webhook status",
-        "Reference: https://www.wappbiz.com/blogs/frequency-capping/ and https://crmsupport.freshworks.com/support/solutions/articles/50000009847"
