-      "title": "Implement OWASP LLM06 â€” vector store access control and embedding partitioning",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "OWASP LLM06:2025 (Vector and Embedding Weaknesses) requires fine-grained access controls on vector databases to prevent cross-tenant data leakage, embedding inversion attacks, and similarity attacks that retrieve unintended content. Rainbow AI serves two properties (Pelangi and Southern) with separate knowledge bases but potentially shared vector infrastructure â€” without logical partitioning, a query for one property could retrieve embeddings from the other.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Vector store queries are scoped by a `property_id` (or `namespace`) tag so Pelangi KB embeddings are never returned in response to Southern queries and vice versa",
-        "Embedding retrieval requires an authenticated service identity; unauthenticated or cross-tenant queries return a 403 and are logged",
-        "Vector DB access logs (query, retrieved doc IDs, scores) are retained for 90 days and accessible in the admin audit trail",
-        "Routine quarterly audit script verifies no cross-namespace vectors exist in the store",
-        "Similarity attack mitigation: queries returning unusually high-score matches to out-of-namespace documents trigger an alert"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Applies to pgvector (Neon) namespace/metadata filtering or any future dedicated vector store",
-        "OWASP recommends 'logical and access-based partitioning of vector datasets to prohibit unauthorized access between user groups'",
-        "Embedding inversion risk: do not expose raw embedding vectors in API responses",
