-      "id": "US-968",
-      "title": "Enforce Malaysia PDPA 2024 data processor Security Principle obligations",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "The Malaysia Personal Data Protection (Amendment) Act 2024, Phase 3 (effective June 2025), directly obliges data processors (including SaaS/chatbot platforms) to comply with the Security Principle: taking practical steps to protect personal data from loss, misuse, modification, unauthorized access, and destruction. Non-compliance carries fines up to RM1 million and/or 3 years imprisonment. Rainbow AI processes guest PII (names, phone numbers, booking data) as both a data controller and processor and must formally document its technical and organizational security measures.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A Data Processing Agreement (DPA) document exists describing Rainbow AI's technical and organizational security measures, aligned with PDPA Section 9",
-        "All PII fields in the database (guest names, phone numbers, booking data) are encrypted at rest using AES-256 or equivalent",
-        "Access to PII is gated by role-based access control; only roles explicitly requiring PII access can query those fields",
-        "A data processing inventory document lists every category of personal data processed, the legal basis, retention period, and security measure applied",
-        "Automated data-retention enforcement deletes or anonymizes guest PII after the configured retention period (default: 2 years post-checkout)",
-        "Security measures are reviewed annually and the review is recorded in the audit log"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "PDPA Amendment 2024 Phase 3 effective June 2025 â€” data processors now directly liable under Security Principle",
