-      "description": "Meta is rolling out an in-app webview experience where CTA links open inside WhatsApp rather than launching an external browser. By end-2025 this is the default for most users. The webchat widget and any external URLs sent by Rainbow AI must be optimised for the WhatsApp webview — fast load, no browser-back dependency, prefilled checkout data — to avoid broken UX when the default behaviour changes.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "All URLs sent by Rainbow AI use HTTPS and render correctly at 390px width (WhatsApp webview default)",
-        "Pages load within 2 seconds inside WhatsApp webview (LCP < 2s measured via Lighthouse on throttled mobile)",
-        "Pages do not rely on browser back-button for navigation — explicit close/back UI controls are present",
-        "Checkout and order confirmation pages prefill customer context (name, order ID) from URL params",
-        "Session continuity: user can minimise webview and resume from same position on re-open"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "WhatsApp webview uses gesture-based navigation; avoid relying on history.back()",
-        "Compress images and defer non-critical JS; target < 150KB initial bundle for webview load",
-        "Test with WhatsApp beta on Android/iOS to verify in-app webview behaviour before release",
-        "Reference: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/cloud-api/guides/send-messages"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
