-    {
-      "id": "US-987",
-      "title": "Implement Malaysia PDPA data minimisation controls in AI prompt construction",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Malaysia's PDPA Section 6 (Collection Principle) requires that personal data collected and processed be adequate but not excessive relative to the stated purpose. Rainbow AI currently passes full guest profiles and conversation histories to AI providers for every intent, including unrelated fields. Implementing a per-intent PII allowlist that strips irrelevant data before LLM calls reduces compliance exposure and shrinks the blast radius of any AI provider data incident.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A per-intent PII allowlist config (JSON file) specifies which data fields may be included in prompts for each intent class",
-        "AI prompt construction strips fields not in the allowlist for the current intent (e.g., passport number is not sent for a menu enquiry)",
-        "Prohibited PII fields (NRIC, passport numbers, full bank account numbers) are replaced with [REDACTED] in all prompts regardless of intent",
-        "An audit log records which PII fields were included in each AI provider call",
-        "Unit tests verify that minimisation rules are applied correctly per intent with no regression"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "PDPA Section 6 Collection Principle: data must be adequate, relevant, and not excessive for the stated purpose",
-        "Config location: src/assistant/data/pii-allowlist.json (intent -> allowed fields mapping)",
-        "Reference: https://www.pdp.gov.my/jpdpv2/assets/2019/09/Personal-Data-Protection-Act-2010.pdf",
-        "Cross-reference with OWASP LLM02 sensitive information disclosure story (already completed) for overlap"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false
-    },
